  "scope": "Propagate the trusted Storyboard root to generated element references and atomically publish or reuse the live identity without overwriting uploaded media.",
  "upstreamExisting": [
    "Element bible/placeholder discovery, image generation, in-step storage and per-entry concurrent durable execution.",
    "Organization wallet reservations, usage, idempotent deduction and provenance.",
    "Immutable element IDs, renameable per-sequence unique tokens, soft deletion and upload/media metadata."
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "UpdateStale overwrites a stale reference payload owner with the explicit resolved root/claim, or an actual Storyboard parent instance-only fallback.",
    "A narrow publisher validates the actual organization/sequence and, when bound, current root or explicitly trusted raw claim plus processing in actual SQL.",
    "Conditional placeholder UPDATE, identity-absent INSERT and final availability SELECT share one atomic D1 batch with rollback on unavailable final result.",
    "ID-first rename behavior, uploaded-media winner precedence, tombstone reservation, initial defaults and placeholder metadata are preserved.",
    "Preflight validates sequence access and actual row relationship through existing named existence hatches; read-site registration follows the extracted helper.",
    "Original generation/storage/accounting/provenance step names, identifiers, metadata, models, language, cap and allSettled behavior remain intact.",
    "Incurred accounting and provenance precede publication refusal. Confirmed root loss is nonretryable inside steps; unknown checks preserve causes; engine abort takes priority across siblings.",
    "A root-bound final durable completion check covers empty output and cached element steps first reaching that check, with explicit cache limits."
  ],
